and Caroline's souls could rest in peace. An overcast sky stretched above the forest, drizzling rain down on the crowds as they let candles and laid wreaths. A Welsh flag was draped over the site where Joanne was found, and some 30 metres away, a Union jack flag lay where Caroline was discovered. The rain began to ease as Anglican Minister Father Stephen Gray began his opening address, declaring, We have come here to this place, a place where something wicked happened, to call on the
