power of God, so this place will be peaceful again. Members of the Sydney Welsh Choir sang a popular folk song from their homeland, Mavunwi. At the conclusion of the service, they sang, You'll Never Walk Alone, during which the clouds parted, and the sun shone down upon the forest. Following the service, Joanne's father said, I just couldn't leave without thanking the Australian people for how they've helped us. To have gone home without this service would have been leaving something out. Now we're putting this area back to how it was, and putting the girls to rest.
悉尼威尔士合唱团的成员们演唱了他们家乡的一首流行民歌《Mavunwi》。在仪式结束时，他们演唱了《你永独行》（You'll Never Walk Alone），期间云开雾散，阳光洒满森林。仪式结束后，乔安妮的父亲说，我只是不能在不感谢澳大利亚人民如何帮助过我们的情况下离开。如果连这个仪式都没有就回家，那就好像有所遗漏。现在我们要把这个地区恢复原貌，让女孩们入土为安。

