on the case full-time was reduced to just three. On October 5, 1993, a little over one year since Joanne Walters and Caroline Clark were found, a local man named De Bruis Pryor was driving through Balingalo in search of firewood. This was something he had always done, but ever since the murders, Bruis remained extra observant while collecting wood on the off chance he came across anything police had missed during their search. On this particular day, Bruis drove along the upper end of the Longacre fire trail. He was in a remote area of dense scrub, located approximately 500 metres from where Joanne
